8006:
General term uses sum of squares as T_r = \frac{1}{r}\frac{r(r+1)(2r+1)}{6} = \frac{(r+1)(2r+1)}{6} = \frac{2r^2+3r+1}{6}
Summing r = 1 to 10 with sums 385 and 55 gives S_{10} = \frac{1}{6}(2 \times 385+3 \times 55+10) = \frac{945}{6}
Simplifying gives \frac{315}{2} → (C)

8009:
After each mixed draw counts drop by one of each colour so successive conditional probabilities multiply
Required probability equals \frac{6}{11} \times \frac{5}{9} \times \frac{4}{7} \times \frac{3}{5} \times \frac{2}{3}
Simplifying gives \frac{16}{231} → (C)

8013:
Left side simplifies as \sin(\tan^{-1}(x\sqrt{2})) = \frac{x\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{1+2x^2}} for x in (0,1)
Right side simplifies as \cot(\sin^{-1}\sqrt{1-x^2}) = \frac{x}{\sqrt{1-x^2}}
Equating and cancelling x gives 2(1-x^2) = 1+2x^2 so x = \frac{1}{2} → (A)

8015:
Put u = 2\vec{a}+3\vec{b} with v = \vec{a}-\vec{b} so u \times v = -5\vec{a} \times \vec{b} and area equals \frac{5}{2}|\vec{a} \times \vec{b}|
Direct computation gives \vec{a} \times \vec{b} = (0,12,-12) with magnitude 12\sqrt{2}
Hence area equals 30\sqrt{2} whose square is 1800 → (C)

8020:
Denominator equals (|x|+1)^2 which is even while x^3 over it is odd so its integral over [-1,1] vanishes
Remaining integrand simplifies to \frac{|x|+1}{(|x|+1)^2} = \frac{1}{|x|+1}
Hence integral equals 2\int_0^1\frac{dx}{x+1} = 2\log_e 2 → (B)

8022:
Factor left side as (1-x)^{10}(1+x+x^2)^{10} and divide to get (1+x+x^2)^{10} = \sum a_r x^r(1-x)^{20-2r}
Setting x = 1 kills all terms except r = 10 giving a_{10} = 3^{10}
Expanding to second order in x = 1+h gives a_9 = 3^{10}\frac{10}{3} so \frac{9a_9}{a_{10}} = 30 → (30)

8028:
Let same force F act at the top with rolling without slipping and a in m/s^{2}
Translation plus rotation give a = 2 F / (M (1 + k)) where I = k M R^{2}
Solid sphere k = 2 / 5 gives a_{A} = 2 F / (7 m) and shell k = 2 / 3 gives a_{B} = 6 F / (5 m)
Ratio a_{A} / a_{B} = 5 / 21, which matches option A → (A)

8032:
Centre of mass velocity is \vec{v}_{cm} = (4 \hat{i} + 4 \hat{j}) / 2 = 2 \hat{i} + 2 \hat{j} in m/s
Similarly \vec{a}_{cm} = (6 \hat{i} + 6 \hat{j}) / 2 = 3 \hat{i} + 3 \hat{j} in m/s^{2}
Since \vec{a}_{cm} is parallel to \vec{v}_{cm} the path is a straight line → (C)

8033:
Young modulus is Y = (W / A) / (\Delta l / L) with Y in N/m^{2}
Graph slope is \Delta l / W = 10^{-5} m/N with L = 1 m and A = 10^{-5} m^{2}
So Y = 1 / (10^{-5} \times 10^{-5}) = 10^{10} N/m^{2} → (C)

8037:
Electric field is the negative gradient with E_{x} = -\partial V / \partial x and E_{y} = -\partial V / \partial y in V/m
With V = 5 (x^{2} - y^{2}) this gives \vec{E} = -10 x \hat{i} + 10 y \hat{j}
At (2, 3) this is -20 \hat{i} + 30 \hat{j} V/m → (A)

8042:
Prism formula gives n = \sin((A + D_{m}) / 2) / \sin(A / 2) with A = 60^{\circ} and D_{m} = 30^{\circ}
Hence n = \sin 45^{\circ} / \sin 30^{\circ} = \frac{1/\sqrt{2}}{1/2} = \sqrt{2}
