Bohr radius follows r = 52.9 \frac{n^{2}}{Z} \text{ pm}
Here \frac{n^{2}}{Z} = \frac{70.53}{52.9} = \frac{4}{3}
Only Z = 3 with n = 2 satisfies this, i.e. \text{Li}^{2+} in n = 2
