8056:
Dissociation \text{A}_{x}\text{B}_{y} \rightleftharpoons x\text{A} + y\text{B} with degree \alpha gives [\text{A}] = xc\alpha and [\text{B}] = yc\alpha
Hence K = \frac{(xc\alpha)^{x}(yc\alpha)^{y}}{c} = c^{x+y-1}x^{x}y^{y}\alpha^{x+y}
Solving gives \alpha = \left(\frac{K}{c^{x+y-1}x^{x}y^{y}}\right)^{\frac{1}{x+y}}
This expression is the listed option → (B)

8060:
First ionisation removes the 4s electron: \text{Mn} 3d^{5}4s^{2} holds it tighter than \text{Cr} 3d^{5}4s^{1}, so \Delta_{i}H_{1} has \text{Mn} > \text{Cr}
Second ionisation removes from \text{Cr}^{+} 3d^{5} half filled shell versus \text{Mn}^{+} 4s^{1}, so \Delta_{i}H_{2} has \text{Cr} > \text{Mn}
Thus only B and C hold, which matches option B → (B)

8063:
In \text{CH}_{3}\text{COOCH}_{3} label \alpha as \text{C=O}, \beta as \text{C-O} and \gamma as \text{O-CH}_{3}
Double bond \alpha is shortest and resonance shortens \beta relative to the pure single bond \gamma
Hence \alpha < \beta < \gamma which is option B → (B)

