Balanced as 2\text{MnO}_{4}^{-} + 6\text{I}^{-} + 4\text{H}_{2}\text{O} \rightarrow 2\text{MnO}_{2} + 3\text{I}_{2} + 8\text{OH}^{-}
Moles \text{MnO}_{4}^{-} equal 0.1, limiting, giving 0.15 mol \text{I}_{2} needing 0.3 mol thiosulphate
With 0.3 \text{ L} consumed, x = \frac{0.3}{0.3} = 1
This value gives → (1)

